Implementation sketch and example snippets included below for reviewers. Copy these into the PR description for runnable examples.

=== Adapter usage example: AsyncIterable -> ReadableStream ===
// convertToReadableStream: (asyncIterable, {strictBackpressure}) => ReadableStream
const stream = convertToReadableStream(async function* () {
  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    // each yield represents a token/chunk produced by an LLM runtime
    yield new TextEncoder().encode(`token-${i}`);
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 4));
  }
}());

// consumer can pipe to fetch request body in browsers or be consumed by TransformStream:
await fetch('/upload', { method: 'POST', body: stream });

=== Adapter usage example: ReadableStream -> AsyncIterable ===
// convertToAsyncIterable: (readable, {abortSignal}) => AsyncIterable<Uint8Array>
async function consume(readable) {
  for await (const chunk of convertToAsyncIterable(readable)) {
    console.log('got', new TextDecoder().decode(chunk));
  }
}

=== Important semantic mappings (we test these explicitly) ===
- readable.cancel(reason) -> iterator.throw(new AbortError(reason)) where possible
- iterator.return() -> controller.close() + ensure pending reads are resolved
- error thrown inside iterator.next() -> stream.error propagated to reader/piped sinks
- single-consumer enforcement: convertToAsyncIterable must throw if multiple consumers attempt iteration (ReadableStream semantics differ across environments)

=== Conformance test matrix (high-level) ===
- chunk boundaries preserved across adapters (no implicit coalescing or splitting)
- backpressure honored: when consumer waits, producer's next() should not be invoked beyond prefetch limit
- cancellation: both sides propagate cancellation and cleanup (timers, open handles)
- error mapping: synchronous and asynchronous throws produce stream errors that bubble to consumer promises
- runtime matrix: Node 18/20, Deno stable, Chrome stable (headless), Bun (smoke)

=== Migration guidance for SDK users ===
- If you used ad-hoc converters, recommend migrating to convertToAsyncIterable/convertToReadableStream for predictable behavior.
- For latency-sensitive paths, set strictBackpressure=true. For throughput-sensitive batch jobs, set relaxedThroughput=true and tune highWaterMark.

